/isomerase superfamily. The protein encoded is a key mitochondrial enzyme involved in beta-oxidation of unsaturated fatty acids. It catalyzes the transformation of 3-cis and 3-trans-enoyl-CoA esters arising during the stepwise degradation of cis-, mono-, and polyunsaturated fatty acids to the 2-trans-enoyl-CoA intermediates. Alternatively spliced transcript variants have been described. [provided by RefSeq, Aug 2011].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O75521","text":"Auxiliary enzyme in the beta-oxidation of mono- and polyunsaturated fatty acids (PubMed:10419495). Together with the 2,4-dienoyl-CoA reductase (DECR) and the Delta(3,5)-Delta(2,4)-dienoyl-CoA isomerase (ECH), they allow the reentrance of the enoyl-CoA into the beta-oxidation cycle (PubMed:10419495). Able to isomerize both 3-cis (3Z) and 3-trans (3E) double bonds into the 2-trans (2E) form in a range of fatty enoyl-CoA species, with a preference for (3E)-enoyl-CoAs over (3Z)-enoyl-CoAs (PubMed:10419495, PubMed:25515061). Based on its established catalytic mechanism, it is predicted to act also on other fatty acids besides those tested experimentally (Probable)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}